## Why This Is Asked
This question tests practical amortized analysis for dynamic frequency tracking, demonstrates how to monitor hot keys efficiently, and contrasts incremental updates with full recomputation.

## Key Concepts
- Amortized analysis for batched updates
- Frequency buckets for O(1) max-frequency queries
- Hash maps for per-label counts
- Sparse vs. dense label domains
- Space-time tradeoff analysis

## Code Example
```javascript
class HotKeyTracker {
  constructor(initialCounts) {
    this.cnt = new Map();
    this.freq = new Map();
    this.maxFreq = 0;
    for (const [k, v] of Object.entries(initialCounts)) {
      this.cnt.set(k, v);
      this.freq.set(v, (this.freq.get(v) || 0) + 1);
      this.maxFreq = Math.max(this.maxFreq, v);
    }
  }

  update(label, delta) {
    const old = this.cnt.get(label) || 0;
    const freqCount = this.freq.get(old) || 0;
    if (freqCount === 1) this.freq.delete(old);
    else this.freq.set(old, freqCount - 1);

    const nw = old + delta;
    this.cnt.set(label, nw);
    this.freq.set(nw, (this.freq.get(nw) || 0) + 1);
    this.maxFreq = Math.max(this.maxFreq, nw);
  }

  hasHotKey(threshold) {
    return this.maxFreq >= threshold;
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests streaming heavy-hitters knowledge, practical analysis of tradeoffs, and ability to reason about accuracy vs memory.\n\n## Key Concepts
- Misra-Gries heavy-hitters algorithm\n- Amortized per-item cost and fixed memory\n- Accuracy guarantees and when top-k is exact vs approximate\n\n## Code Example
```javascript
class MGHeavyHitters {
  constructor(k) {
    this.k = k; // top-k to track
    this.counters = new Map(); // id -> count
  }
  add(x) {
    if (this.counters.has(x)) {
      this.counters.set(x, this.counters.get(x) + 1);
    } else if (this.counters.size < this.k - 1) {
      this.counters.set(x, 1);
    } else {
      // decrement all counters
      for (let [id, cnt] of Array.from(this.counters)) {
        if (cnt === 1) this.counters.delete(id);
        else this.counters.set(id, cnt - 1);
      }
    }
  }
}
```
